    "raw": "Given:\n- Speed with 200 people = 500 km/hr\n- For every 100 additional people, the speed is halved\n\nTo find:\n- Speed with 400 people on board\n\nFirst, let's identify the increase in the number of people:\n- From 200 to 400 people, there is an increase of 200 people.\n\nNext, we need to determine how many 100-person increments are in this increase:\n- 200 people / 100 people per increment = 2 increments\n\nSince the speed is halved for each 100 additional people, we need to halve the speed twice:\n- First halving: 500 km/hr / 2 = 250 km/hr\n- Second halving: 250 km/hr / 2 = 125 km/hr\n\nThus, the speed of the spaceship with 400 people on board is 125 km/hr.\n\nFINAL: 125",
